1
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:32,330
[panting]

2
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:33,540
There you are!

3
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:35,210
- [panting]
- Anne!

4
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:36,830
I'm so glad to see
that you're safe!

5
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,040
It's Challe!
He needs help, now!

6
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,250
Hurry, or Lafalle's
going to kill him!

7
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:44,790
Please, Lusul. Please!

8
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:46,460
[grunts]

9
00:01:46,790 --> 00:01:47,790
[gasps]

10
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,880
♪

11
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:57,630
[groaning]

12
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:01,790
Is it painful?

13
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:04,460
That's your punishment
for insulting me

14
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:06,170
and taking the side of a human.

15
00:02:07,790 --> 00:02:08,630
[scoffs]

16
00:02:08,710 --> 00:02:11,710
[groaning]

17
00:02:13,290 --> 00:02:14,710
This is so pitiful.

18
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:18,750
Why did I believe that we could
respect each other as kings

19
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,040
or that you and I
could love each other?

20
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:22,710
- [grunts]
- [LAFALLE] How did things

21
00:02:22,790 --> 00:02:23,920
turn out so ugly?

22
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:25,830
- [grunts]
- [LAFALLE] Oh, I know.

23
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,330
Humanity is to blame
for all of it!

24
00:02:29,670 --> 00:02:32,500
[groans]

25
00:02:33,250 --> 00:02:34,290
[MALE FAIRY 22A]
Master Lafalle!

26
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:35,460
Hm.

27
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,750
We've captured
the human girl for you.

28
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:40,330
- [gasps]
- Skillfully done.

29
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:43,210
Pay attention.

30
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,000
I want you to see what happens

31
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:47,080
to your dear
Silver Sugar Master.

32
00:02:47,290 --> 00:02:50,290
[groaning]

33
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:53,920
This human dared
to stand between us.

34
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,630
- Anne!
- And now she'll pay.

35
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,460
- Stop it!
- [gasps]

36
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:03,830
You little pest!

37
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,330
♪

38
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:06,580
[shattering]

39
00:03:07,130 --> 00:03:08,670
Your wing! I've got it here!

40
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,960
- Thank you.
- How dare you! [gasps]

41
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:14,290
What are you doing?

42
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:16,290
Master Lafalle,

43
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:18,130
please let this girl go free.

44
00:03:18,210 --> 00:03:20,080
I know she's a human,
but she's kind!

45
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:22,920
You would defy me for her?

46
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,830
- [screams]
- [swords clanking]

47
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:28,040
Anne! Get out of here, now!

48
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:30,380
All of you! Hurry!

49
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,710
- Take Anne with you!
- [gasps] Challe!

50
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:35,630
You've all betrayed me!

51
00:03:35,710 --> 00:03:37,170
[screams]

52
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:38,460
[swords clanking]

53
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:40,170
♪

54
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:45,380
[swords clanking]

55
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:48,540
[grunting]

56
00:03:50,210 --> 00:03:51,130
[chuckles]

57
00:03:51,210 --> 00:03:53,630
♪

58
00:03:54,670 --> 00:03:55,710
Lafalle!

59
00:03:57,170 --> 00:03:58,040
[chuckles]

60
00:04:00,790 --> 00:04:01,790
[grunts]

61
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:04,960
- [rumbling]
- [clattering]

62
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:08,630
[grunts]

63
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:12,420
[Lafalle laughing]

64
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:16,380
Aren't you a pathetic sight?

65
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,210
Now come here.

66
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:21,080
[grunts]

67
00:04:32,170 --> 00:04:33,170
[gasps]

68
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:36,330
[wind whooshing]

69
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:44,580
Good.

70
00:04:44,670 --> 00:04:46,250
♪

71
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:49,080
This is the end,
Challe Fen Challe!

72
00:04:49,170 --> 00:04:50,670
[horse neighing]

73
00:04:50,830 --> 00:04:51,830
[gasps]

74
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:54,500
[wind whooshing]

75
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:57,580
[clip-clopping]

76
00:04:58,540 --> 00:05:01,540
[wind whooshing]

77
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:03,170
The humans found us.

78
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:04,630
How's that possible?

79
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:07,330
I see. About time.

80
00:05:07,670 --> 00:05:08,670
Huh?

81
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:11,880
[wind whooshing]

82
00:05:12,790 --> 00:05:13,920
It was you then.

83
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:15,500
Of course.

84
00:05:15,630 --> 00:05:17,250
♪

85
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:21,630
I'm being betrayed
by my own allies, once again.

86
00:05:23,290 --> 00:05:24,380
Of all people...

87
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:27,290
it's you.

88
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:30,170
After you'd taken my wing,

89
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:32,630
you were the person
controlling me.

90
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:34,790
You're not my ally,

91
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:37,000
so this is not a betrayal.

92
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:41,460
A year ago, I met
a 15-year-old human girl

93
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:42,830
who understood the difference.

94
00:05:43,710 --> 00:05:45,420
And yet you still can't.

95
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:49,250
[LAFALLE] If I had been able
to find you before you met her,

96
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,500
do you think you would have
turned your blade

97
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:54,250
against me the way you are now?

98
00:05:55,170 --> 00:05:56,210
[CHALLE]
Probably not.

99
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:59,130
But then such is fate.

100
00:05:59,330 --> 00:06:00,290
[chuckles]

101
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:03,580
I see. Fate.

102
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,920
It's over, Lafalle.

103
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:11,920
♪

104
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:16,420
[gasps]

105
00:06:17,790 --> 00:06:18,830
[gasps]

106
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,920
[wind whooshing]

107
00:06:30,290 --> 00:06:32,170
- [LUSUL] Wait, Anne!
- [all gasp]

108
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:33,290
What's the matter?

109
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,210
The humans!

110
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:39,380
Soldiers? But why?

111
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:41,250
[gasps]

112
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:43,960
You can't!

113
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:46,130
I know you're all strong,

114
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:47,920
but there are too many
troops coming!

115
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:49,880
- [CHALLE] Anne is right.
- [gasps]

116
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:53,080
Don't throw your lives away.

117
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:54,290
You're here!

118
00:06:58,710 --> 00:06:59,670
Oh, Challe.
[sobs]

119
00:06:59,750 --> 00:07:00,580
You're all right!

120
00:07:01,130 --> 00:07:04,080
Challe!
[crying]

121
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:06,130
I'm glad you're safe as well.

122
00:07:07,630 --> 00:07:09,500
[LUSUL]
Lafalle? What happened?

123
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,080
[Anne crying]

124
00:07:13,130 --> 00:07:14,630
[CHALLE]
He fell from the walls.

125
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:17,960
That's awful to hear.

126
00:07:18,790 --> 00:07:21,250
♪

127
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:22,880
[Lusul grunts]

128
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:26,750
I have recovered the chest
containing all of your wings.

129
00:07:27,790 --> 00:07:29,790
Take them,
escape through the back gate.

130
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:30,920
[all gasp]

131
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,460
[indistinct chatter]

132
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:33,500
Thank you.

133
00:07:33,630 --> 00:07:35,170
But now we've lost our king.

134
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:36,960
We'd be ever so grateful

135
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,790
if you would become
our king instead.

136
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:41,580
You don't need a king.

137
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,000
You are free now.

138
00:07:43,540 --> 00:07:45,710
Your futures
are for each of you to decide.

139
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:49,630
♪

140
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:50,920
This is the fortress.

141
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:52,380
But Anne Halford's in there.

142
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,920
Milord, please be cautious.

143
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,170
I understand that.

144
00:07:56,630 --> 00:07:59,080
Sadly, considering
all the violence

145
00:07:59,170 --> 00:08:00,710
that these fairies
have committed,

146
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:02,630
we can't afford to hold back.

147
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:04,420
Hm?

148
00:08:06,210 --> 00:08:09,040
[LUSUL] I had no idea
my wing was beautiful.

149
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,540
I only realized it
when you said it was.

150
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:15,250
It made me feel so very proud.

151
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,750
[grunts]

152
00:08:19,250 --> 00:08:21,670
I've chosen
to journey on with him.

153
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:24,250
I would like to see
the ocean too!

154
00:08:25,170 --> 00:08:26,210
Farewell, friends!

155
00:08:30,790 --> 00:08:31,790
I wonder...

156
00:08:32,670 --> 00:08:33,750
if she'll make it there.

157
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:37,790
Fairies born from plants
don't live for long.

158
00:08:38,130 --> 00:08:39,250
Usually a year.

159
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:43,710
But then she did consume
your sugar confections.

160
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:46,000
I'm sure she'll see the ocean.

161
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:48,460
Hm?

162
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:50,630
♪

163
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:05,630
[ANNE]
I hope you're right.

164
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,290
[door creaks]

165
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:14,670
- [gasps] Anne!
- [gasps]

166
00:09:15,630 --> 00:09:16,580
There you are!

167
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,920
I missed you, Mithril Lid Pod!

168
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:23,000
Anne! You're all right!
You had me so worried!

169
00:09:23,130 --> 00:09:25,000
I'm sorry,
everything's fine now.

170
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,920
- [heavy footsteps]
- [both gasp]

171
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:28,750
[panting]

172
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,540
[sighs]
You two!

173
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,540
You sure keep us on our toes.

174
00:09:33,630 --> 00:09:34,540
I'll give you that.

175
00:09:35,290 --> 00:09:37,540
You're here at last!

176
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:40,540
We've really missed you,
all of you.

177
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:42,920
Oh, Orland.

178
00:09:43,330 --> 00:09:45,290
I'm doing fine.
Please don't worry.

179
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:47,920
What about yourself?
I do hope you're unharmed.

180
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:49,250
Yes!

181
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:51,830
[KAT] Would you all dispense
with the dramatics?

182
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:53,210
This is silly.

183
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:55,630
I told you that she would
come back here, didn't I?

184
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:58,460
I appreciate it, Kat and Jonas.

185
00:09:58,710 --> 00:09:59,750
Thank you!

186
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,580
Huh? Kieth?

187
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,750
Welcome back, Anne, Challe.

188
00:10:04,130 --> 00:10:05,790
It's good to see
that you're both safe.

189
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,960
What are you doing here
at Paige, Kieth?

190
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:09,830
I was helping them all
with the work.

191
00:10:10,290 --> 00:10:12,460
What about Mr. Radcliffe?

192
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:13,960
It's fine.

193
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:16,330
I considered
my choice carefully

194
00:10:17,830 --> 00:10:20,710
Oh, Mr. Collins, the project!

195
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,080
How is it progressing?

196
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:24,330
It's straight back
to work, huh?

197
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:27,250
Your first thought is always
about your sugar confections.

198
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:29,460
Come, look.

199
00:10:30,290 --> 00:10:31,880
[gasps]

200
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:35,000
♪

201
00:10:35,170 --> 00:10:36,290
I'm speechless.

202
00:10:36,750 --> 00:10:38,920
- You did so much!
- I know.

203
00:10:39,210 --> 00:10:40,710
- Every piece is here.
- [chuckles]

204
00:10:40,790 --> 00:10:42,170
- Just as you ordered.
- What?

205
00:10:43,170 --> 00:10:44,040
But the...

206
00:10:44,210 --> 00:10:46,080
The festival is ten days away.

207
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:48,130
We finished with time to spare?

208
00:10:48,330 --> 00:10:49,920
Yes.

209
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,080
[laughs]

210
00:10:51,580 --> 00:10:52,960
[NADIR] The whole time
you were gone,

211
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,920
the image of our amazing
Head of Artisans

212
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,080
wouldn't leave our minds!

213
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:58,790
[KING] We might've gotten
a little carried away.

214
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:00,460
[VALENTINE]
This is all thanks to you.

215
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:03,290
[ANNE] They did it.
They're all so wonderful!

216
00:11:03,630 --> 00:11:07,210
Everything looks perfect,
and it's done early!

217
00:11:07,830 --> 00:11:09,170
[gasps]

218
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,580
Mr. Collins,
if we still have ten days left,

219
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:15,170
perhaps there's something more
we can do.

220
00:11:15,830 --> 00:11:17,750
I've been thinking
that same thing, Anne.

221
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:19,630
So, you're in charge.

222
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:21,250
Have an idea?

223
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:23,170
[VALENTINE] We'd better
stick to snowflakes.

224
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:25,290
Nothing else would match,
you know?

225
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:28,170
That's true, but just
adding more of them

226
00:11:28,250 --> 00:11:29,580
seems kind of boring.

227
00:11:29,710 --> 00:11:30,880
If we're going to do something,

228
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:33,710
then we might as well make it
as big and bold as possible!

229
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:34,960
I think so, too.

230
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:36,580
Let's make it count.

231
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:40,040
♪

232
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:45,750
All right! We'll make it bold!

233
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:48,330
[all cheering]

234
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:54,170
You'd like to start bringing
the pieces three days early?

235
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:55,750
If you don't mind.

236
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:57,790
We've done everything
except assemble them.

237
00:11:58,460 --> 00:12:00,630
I promise, it'll be
the grandest decoration

238
00:12:00,710 --> 00:12:03,000
the Holy Beginnings Festival
has ever had!

239
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:04,380
Hmm.

240
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:06,920
[BRIDGET]
What are you doing?

241
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:08,830
Miss Bridget, it's you.

242
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:12,380
I'm just looking at the moon,
nothing more.

243
00:12:13,290 --> 00:12:14,670
- You might catch a cold.
- [gasps]

244
00:12:17,170 --> 00:12:18,170
Is that...?

245
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:20,130
I just never got to return it.

246
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,080
[chuckles]

247
00:12:28,210 --> 00:12:29,170
By the way,

248
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:31,790
I broke off my engagement
to Mr. Collins.

249
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:32,920
Huh?

250
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,420
What happened?

251
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,040
Like you said,

252
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:38,880
I should think about
what I can do now,

253
00:12:40,210 --> 00:12:42,290
and in my current
circumstances.

254
00:12:43,210 --> 00:12:45,130
I tended to Orland's injuries,

255
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:47,460
then watched over the others.

256
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:49,960
It made me realize something.

257
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,500
I truly love this workshop,

258
00:12:54,170 --> 00:12:56,330
and I love every person
who's a part of it.

259
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:59,250
Elliott is a brilliant artisan.

260
00:12:59,830 --> 00:13:02,210
So, when my father suggested
we get engaged,

261
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:04,000
I didn't object at all.

262
00:13:04,710 --> 00:13:05,880
But the truth is,

263
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:08,920
I didn't do that
because I desired to.

264
00:13:09,630 --> 00:13:11,250
I was just suffocating,
in a way.

265
00:13:12,630 --> 00:13:14,630
I told my father
he should take Elliott in

266
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:17,330
as an adopted son and let him
take over the workshop.

267
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:20,960
That would be best for Paige.

268
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:23,290
And best for me, as well.

269
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:26,790
Oh, how did Mr. Glen respond?

270
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:28,960
He fully understood it all.

271
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,670
And Elliott said,

272
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,630
"Bridget's demands
usually cause me

273
00:13:32,710 --> 00:13:34,420
a great deal
of grief and headache.

274
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:36,580
But for the first time,
I am inclined

275
00:13:36,670 --> 00:13:37,710
to go along with them!"

276
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,000
Word for word.

277
00:13:39,330 --> 00:13:40,330
Hm.

278
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:43,880
[laughs] That does sound like
something he would say!

279
00:13:44,250 --> 00:13:45,250
Right?

280
00:13:45,330 --> 00:13:48,080
[both laughing]

281
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:54,710
[KING] All that's left
is the Paige Workshop finale!

282
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:56,080
Hm.

283
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,500
[laughs]

284
00:13:58,330 --> 00:13:59,420
Time to begin!

285
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,170
Start with the biggest!

286
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:02,750
Two of the white flakes!

287
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:12,880
♪

288
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:52,130
[snoring]

289
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:15,880
- [CHALLE] Anne.
- [gasps]

290
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Challe.

291
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:21,130
You're awake? Why?

292
00:15:22,710 --> 00:15:24,130
I don't know, I couldn't sleep.

293
00:15:24,830 --> 00:15:25,830
Oh, well.

294
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:32,040
I'm confused.

295
00:15:33,330 --> 00:15:35,420
Lafalle said that
he was the fairy king.

296
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:38,170
And he said
you were the fairy king too.

297
00:15:39,330 --> 00:15:40,330
How is that?

298
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:43,580
Apparently,

299
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:47,130
we were both born
from stones gathered by Riselva

300
00:15:47,210 --> 00:15:48,880
to produce the next fairy king.

301
00:15:49,830 --> 00:15:52,790
Or at least,
that's what Lafalle thought.

302
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:55,250
If that's true, then you're...?

303
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:58,710
I don't know if it means
anything for me at all,

304
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:03,330
but either way,
becoming a king isn't easy.

305
00:16:04,790 --> 00:16:07,040
Perhaps the time will come
when I'll need to take

306
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:08,290
some kind of action,

307
00:16:09,040 --> 00:16:10,080
but not now.

308
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:13,460
[ANNE]
Then, what is it time for?

309
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,710
What are you going to do?

310
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:18,420
Keep my promise.

311
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:21,330
Stay with you.

312
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,330
So, you can be happy

313
00:16:25,750 --> 00:16:28,000
and free to live your life
to the fullest.

314
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:31,790
I'll be at your side... forever.

315
00:16:33,250 --> 00:16:34,500
Do as you please to.

316
00:16:35,130 --> 00:16:36,250
Go where you wish,

317
00:16:37,210 --> 00:16:39,250
find someone you love.

318
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:43,380
I'll support you, Anne.

319
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,500
[ANNE]
Someone... I love?

320
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:49,960
♪

321
00:16:52,290 --> 00:16:53,380
[ANNE]
Thank you, Challe.

322
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:58,130
But if I ever did end up
being perfectly happy one day,

323
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:01,210
there'd be no reason left
for you to protect me.

324
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,080
So, Challe...

325
00:17:05,290 --> 00:17:06,330
if that happens,

326
00:17:06,670 --> 00:17:10,170
then it'll be your turn
to live a good life.

327
00:17:11,290 --> 00:17:12,920
Do as you please to,

328
00:17:13,750 --> 00:17:15,170
go where you wish,

329
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,960
and find someone you love,
as well.

330
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:21,960
To be honest, I wish
you could do that now, but...

331
00:17:24,330 --> 00:17:25,460
I'm sorry, Challe.

332
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:27,830
I've caused a lot of trouble
for you.

333
00:17:29,710 --> 00:17:30,960
Forever means?

334
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:32,920
Huh?

335
00:17:33,670 --> 00:17:36,670
Well... if that's what
you truly want.

336
00:17:39,130 --> 00:17:41,960
Now finish the final piece
of your work

337
00:17:42,710 --> 00:17:44,710
and bring good fortune
to the whole kingdom,

338
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:46,000
just as you planned.

339
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:50,380
Right.

340
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:53,920
[ANNE]
The fairy king considered

341
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,500
King Cedric to be a friend,

342
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:59,000
and Cedric saw the fairy king
as a friend, just the same.

343
00:18:00,670 --> 00:18:03,630
Side by side, the two rulers
searched for a path

344
00:18:03,710 --> 00:18:05,960
that humans and fairies
could walk together.

345
00:18:06,790 --> 00:18:09,080
Sadly, that dream
never came true.

346
00:18:09,790 --> 00:18:12,000
But Cedric had crafted
sugar confections

347
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:13,250
for the late Riselva,

348
00:18:14,170 --> 00:18:16,000
and those creations
gained the power

349
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:17,330
to bring good fortune.

350
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:20,170
♪

351
00:18:20,250 --> 00:18:21,500
[ANNE]
I'll place it up high,

352
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:25,170
so that the prosperity
this sugar confection attracts

353
00:18:25,250 --> 00:18:28,040
will reach every person
who resides in this kingdom.

354
00:18:30,290 --> 00:18:32,040
Bring blessings to each human

355
00:18:32,710 --> 00:18:34,580
and each fairy, as well!

356
00:18:39,250 --> 00:18:41,250
[MALE PRIEST 24A]
Happy New Year to all!

357
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:44,790
May fortune smile upon you

358
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,330
and your loved ones.

359
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:47,380
Ha!

360
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:50,880
♪

361
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,170
- [Anne gasps]
- [people laughing]

362
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:03,330
- It's beautiful.
- So beautiful.

363
00:19:03,420 --> 00:19:04,880
- [gasps]
- My word!

364
00:19:05,460 --> 00:19:08,080
With that scale, you would
assume it was built right here!

365
00:19:09,170 --> 00:19:11,040
And the arrangement
of the lighting.

366
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:13,630
It's turned the church
into a snowy landscape!

367
00:19:14,250 --> 00:19:15,250
It's true.

368
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:17,920
Sugar confections
are wonderful!

369
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:20,540
Such great potential!

370
00:19:22,830 --> 00:19:26,000
♪

371
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:27,540
[HUGH]
I'd call that a success.

372
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:28,920
[gasps]

373
00:19:29,250 --> 00:19:30,250
Hugh.

374
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:33,460
This will be a resurgence
for the Paige Workshop.

375
00:19:33,790 --> 00:19:35,080
They'll be quite busy soon.

376
00:19:35,290 --> 00:19:36,330
I'm so glad!

377
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:38,420
I see. Glad.

378
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:41,790
Does this mean you're content
with just that, then?

379
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:43,290
Huh?

380
00:19:43,380 --> 00:19:45,670
If you, Anne Halford,
plan to continue working

381
00:19:45,750 --> 00:19:48,380
in the same capacity at Paige,
that's perfectly fine.

382
00:19:48,710 --> 00:19:50,460
But what does
Silver Sugar Master

383
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:52,210
Anne Halford think about it?

384
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,420
[HUGH] You've yet
to accomplish a single thing

385
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:55,790
that's purely for yourself.

386
00:19:57,380 --> 00:19:58,580
Pardon me, Viscount.

387
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:01,500
Are you flirting
with my Head of Artisans here?

388
00:20:01,790 --> 00:20:03,080
I'd intended to,

389
00:20:03,460 --> 00:20:05,540
but your prattling
would be too exhausting.

390
00:20:06,170 --> 00:20:07,460
I suppose I'll be going.

391
00:20:08,630 --> 00:20:09,960
[ANNE]
I hadn't thought about it.

392
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:12,170
I knew I'd stay with Paige

393
00:20:12,250 --> 00:20:13,790
until the
Holy Beginnings Festival.

394
00:20:14,330 --> 00:20:16,750
But now that that's over,
I'm not so sure.

395
00:20:18,250 --> 00:20:20,750
What do I want
as a Silver Sugar Master?

396
00:20:22,380 --> 00:20:24,330
Let me guess,
the Viscount must've put

397
00:20:24,420 --> 00:20:25,830
another idea into your head.

398
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:27,830
So, what's the plan?

399
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:29,880
Uh, well, you see...

400
00:20:30,210 --> 00:20:31,210
[chuckles]

401
00:20:32,170 --> 00:20:34,830
Look, Anne, you've done
more for us than you can know.

402
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:37,380
Thank you for everything.

403
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:40,500
In return,
here's a bit of advice!

404
00:20:41,210 --> 00:20:42,580
If you're planning
for your future,

405
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,380
I'd say you should build up
even more experience.

406
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,920
The Paige Workshop
is a small world.

407
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:51,670
If you want to become
the best artisan you can be,

408
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:54,380
there's more for you out there.

409
00:20:55,210 --> 00:20:56,330
Mister Collins.

410
00:20:57,830 --> 00:21:00,210
Well, formalities aside.

411
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:03,130
If you ever feel like
things just aren't working out,

412
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:05,500
we will always have
a place for you here.

413
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:39,580
I think I might leave
the Paige Workshop.

414
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:42,790
If you do, then what?

415
00:21:43,250 --> 00:21:44,130
Huh?

416
00:21:44,210 --> 00:21:45,920
What are you planning
to do next?

417
00:21:46,330 --> 00:21:47,920
Back to selling
sugar confections

418
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,000
out of your wagon?

419
00:21:49,670 --> 00:21:51,670
Oh! Um, well, I don't know.

420
00:21:51,750 --> 00:21:52,880
Possibly?

421
00:21:53,420 --> 00:21:55,580
As expected,
you started talking

422
00:21:55,670 --> 00:21:57,250
without thinking
through it first.

423
00:21:57,500 --> 00:21:59,460
Once a scarecrow,
always a scarecrow.

424
00:21:59,750 --> 00:22:01,500
I mean, I have thought
about it a little!

425
00:22:01,580 --> 00:22:02,670
[CHALLE]
Do as you wish.

426
00:22:03,630 --> 00:22:04,630
Huh?

427
00:22:08,210 --> 00:22:09,750
I'll follow you anywhere.

428
00:22:11,130 --> 00:22:12,130
Thank you.

429
00:22:12,420 --> 00:22:14,750
- And I'll be there too!
- [laughs]

430
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:17,080
You're not leaving
without the magnificence

431
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:18,830
that is Lord Mithril Lid Pod!

432
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:20,500
Great!

